<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tepelenë</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tepelena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tepelenë is a town in southern Albania on the Vjosa river, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjirokaster">Gjirokastër</a> County. It was the birthplace and family seat of Ali Pasha, who ruled much of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Ioannina</a> and rebuilt its castle. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-byron">Lord Byron</a> visited him there in 1809 and described the visit in his poem Childe Harold's Pilgrimage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tepelene.jpg" alt="Tepelenë" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albinfo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tepelena_Castle_and_New_Town.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
